SUMMARY:[Cedar] Fixed: Outage - Panne
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20201117T044000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20201117T085700
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-524@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:UNPLANNED
DESCRIPTION:Update:\nWe replaced the failed switch\; we needed to cycle ce
 rtain services and validate consistency during bringing services back onli
 ne. As such\, while most research will have continued uninterrupted\, some
  might have reached timeout due to waiting on services during the outage.\
 nThanks for your patience.\nOriginal:\nCedar is currently offline due to a
  switch failure. We are investigating and work is underway to restore serv
 ices. Will update when more is known.\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/vie
 w_incident?incident=524
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=524
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Graham] Reduced Power Capacity - Capacité De Puissance Réduite
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20201126T192100
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20210125T052500
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-526@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:UNPLANNED
DESCRIPTION:The cluster has been set to drain and some jobs unfortunately 
 terminated in order to lower the overall electrical load in the data centr
 e. Once the load returns to acceptable levels most of the cluster will be 
 returned to service. There is an ongoing project to increase the overall e
 lectrical capacity of the room which is expected to be completed in early 
 2021. Once complete the expansion will prevent this issue from reoccurring
 .\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=526
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=526
END:VEVENT
