BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[DRAC] Arbutus Cloud – Outage for Upgrade\, March 23-26 2021
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20210323T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20210323T120000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-574@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:UPDATE:\nThe upgrade process is now complete\, and all cloud s
 ervices are fully available.\n-- The Arbutus Cloud will undergo a maintena
 nce window to upgrade the cloud infrastructure software.\nThis upgrade wil
 l require a complete outage of the dashboard and API services from 11:00AM
  EDT on March 23rd\, 2021 to 11:00AM EDT on March 24th\, 2021.\nThe upgrad
 e will also require short network outages of less than 10 minutes for each
  Virtual Machine hosted in the Arbutus Cloud during the period from 11:00A
 M EDT on March 24th\, 2021 to 11:00AM EDT on March 26th\, 2021. While netw
 ork connectivity may be interrupted\, affected VMs are not expected to go 
 down or reboot as a result of the upgrade.\nThis outage will also be commu
 nicated on the Compute Canada Status site\, https://status.computecanada.c
 a – please refer to that site to view any updates to this message or cha
 nges that may arise during the course of the maintenance work.\nIf you hav
 e any questions or concerns\, please contact the Compute Canada Cloud Nati
 onal Team:\n[email protected] - Cloud National Team\n---\nDes travaux de 
 maintenance sont prévus pour la mise à jour de l‘infrastructure logici
 elle du nuage Arbutus.\nEntre le 23 mars 11 h HAE et le 24 mars 2021 11
  h HAE\, les travaux nécessiteront la mise hors service complète du ta
 bleau de bord et des services API .\nEntre le 24 mars 11 h HAE et le 26 
 mars 2021 11 h HAE\, il y aura une brève interruption du réseau (moins
  de 10 minutes) pour chacune des instances sur Arbutus. Nous ne prévoyons
  pas que les instances touchées devront être redémarrées.\nVous pouvez
  consulter la page d’état des systèmes https://status.calculcanada.ca 
 pour connaître les détails sur cet arrêt de service.\nSi vous avez des 
 questions\, veuillez écrire à l'équipe nationale des services infonuagi
 ques de la fédération Calcul Canada à [email protected] .\nL'équipe n
 ationale des services infonuagiques\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_
 incident?incident=574
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=574
END:VEVENT
