BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Arbutus] Minor: DNSSEC queries temporarily disabled on cloud recu
 rsive DNS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20211203T202100
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20211206T194800
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-682@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:UNPLANNED
DESCRIPTION:DNSSEC queries are currently disabled on all internal cloud DN
 S servers\, pending a system update after which DNSSEC functionality will 
 be re-enabled. These servers are automatically offered by DHCP to tenant V
 Ms\, and are commonly configured in /etc/resolv.conf.\nIf you rely on zone
  validation\, please use alternative recursive DNS instead.\nAll other que
 ry types will continue to be answered as before.\nIf you have questions\, 
 please open a ticket via [email protected]\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.
 ca/view_incident?incident=682
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=682
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Niagara] Planned Maintenance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20211208T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20211208T153000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-683@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:On Wednesday December 8\, 2021\, at 2:30 PM ET\, maintenance w
 ork on the firewall at the SciNet datacenter will be performed. Datacenter
  external connections will be interrupted for approximately 30 minutes.\nD
 uring this period\, there will be no access to Niagara\, Mist\, Rouge\, HP
 SS\, or the Teach cluster. Jobs in the queue will continue to run\, and ac
 cess should return by 3:00 PM EST.\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_i
 ncident?incident=683
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=683
END:VEVENT
