BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[DRAC] Emergency maintenance shutdown on Friday January 7\, 2022
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20220107T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20220108T000000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-688@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:Over the holidays\, one of the physical components of the file
  systems for the SciNet compute clusters (Niagara\, Mist\, Rouge and Teach
 ) has failed. Although built-in redundancy has allowed the systems to cont
 inue to operate\, a second component failure could be detrimental.\nAn eme
 rgency shutdown of all SciNet to replace this component is planned to take
  place on Friday January 7\, 2022\, and will require at least 12 hours of 
 downtime. Updates on the downtime will be sent out closer to the date.\nPl
 ease check https://docs.scinet.utoronto.ca or https://status.computecanada
 .ca for updates and details.\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_inciden
 t?incident=688
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=688
END:VEVENT
