BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[DRAC] System Outage March 21 - Arrêt de service de la grappe Ced
 ar le 21 mars
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20220321T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20220322T000000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-737@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:System Outage March 21\n-------------------------------\nThe C
 edar system will be unavailable starting March 21 for system updates:\nope
 rating system\, filesystem software\, OmniPath drivers\, scheduler softwar
 e.\nJobs submitted with a runtime request that would extend into the downt
 ime will not start before the downtime.\nFor information see: https://docs
 .computecanada.ca/wiki/Cedar Email [email protected] for assistance and/o
 r to report problems.\nArrêt de service de la grappe Cedar le 21 mars\n--
 --------------------------------------------\nLa grappe Cedar ne sera pas 
 disponible à compter du 21 mars alors que nous effectuerons les mises à 
 jour suivantes : système d’exploitation\, logiciel des systèmes de fic
 hiers\, pilotes OmniPath\, ordonnanceur. Les tâches soumises avec une lim
 ite de temps qui chevauche la période d’arrêt ne démarreront pas avan
 t le retour en service.\nPour plus d’information\, lisez : https://docs.
 computecanada.ca/wiki/Cedar Écrivez à [email protected] pour obtenir de
  l’aide ou rapporter un problème.\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view
 _incident?incident=737
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=737
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[DRAC] Planned Outage - Arrêt planifié
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20220328T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20220328T110000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-741@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:Starting Monday\, March 28th\, 2022\, at 10 am ET\, the Graham
  cluster will be unavailable to all users as we perform regular maintenanc
 e. Running jobs will be terminated. The work will be completed by Tuesday\
 , March 29th\, 2022 at 10 am. During this maintenance window we will be up
 grading the scratch file system.\nPlease watch http://status.computecanada
 .ca for updates on the availability of Graham and all other national syste
 ms.\nWe are upgrading the scratch file system to provide better overall pe
 rformance. The upgrade is not expected to impact any files stored on scrat
 ch\; however\, as with any file system maintenance\, issues could potentia
 lly arise. Therefore\, users are encouraged to copy any critical data stor
 ed on scratch to another filesystem ahead of this maintenance.\nAs a gener
 al reminder: the scratch file system is intended for temporary files\; not
 hing that can’t be recovered or recreated. The scratch file system is no
 t backed up.\nThis outage will impact the cluster\, login nodes\, visualiz
 ation nodes (VDI) as well as data transfer nodes (DTN). There will be no i
 mpact to the Graham cloud.\nStart Time : 10 am ET\, Monday\, March 28\, 20
 22 Anticipated End Time : 10 am ET\, Tuesday\, March 29\, 2022 Users will 
 be notified by email when the cluster is up and running again.\nFor questi
 ons\, or assistance migrating to other national systems\, please email [em
 ail protected] Thank you\, Graham Team\, Compute Canada Federation\n\nhtt
 ps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=741
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=741
END:VEVENT
