BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[DRAC] Planned Outage - Arrêt planifié
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20220525T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20220525T100000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-761@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:Starting Wednesday\, May 25th\, 2022\, at 9 am ET\, the Graham
  cluster will be unavailable to all users as we perform an upgrade of the 
 project file system. All running jobs will be terminated but queued jobs w
 ill remain. Queued jobs that would extend past the beginning of the outage
  will not be allowed to launch until after the maintenance.  The work wil
 l be completed by Thursday\, May 26th\, 2022 at 10 am.\nAt this time we wi
 ll also reduce the maximum job duration to 7 days on Graham. This is the s
 ame scheduler configuration as the Narval and Beluga clusters. Cedar will 
 continue to accept jobs with a duration of more than 7 days.\nPlease watch
  https://status.computecanada.ca for updates on the availability of Graham
  and all other national systems.\nWe are upgrading the project file system
  to provide better overall performance. The upgrade is not expected to cau
 se data loss\; however\, as with any file system maintenance\, issues coul
 d potentially arise. Should issues arise\, we could recover files from the
  daily backups.\nThis outage will impact the cluster\, login nodes\, visua
 lization nodes (VDI) as well as data transfer nodes (DTN). There will be n
 o impact to the Graham cloud.\nStart Time: 9 am ET\, Wednesday\, May 25\, 
 2022 Anticipated End Time: 10 am ET\, Thursday\, May 26\, 2022 Users will 
 be notified by email when the cluster is up and running again.\nFor questi
 ons\, or assistance migrating to other national systems\, please email [em
 ail protected]\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=76
 1
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=761
END:VEVENT
