BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Graham] /scratch filesystem slowness
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20240703T014600
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20241025T153800
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-1140@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:UNPLANNED
DESCRIPTION:You may experience slowness with the /scratch filesystem.\nIt 
 is not broken\, but heavily loaded.  In addition to normal user load\, we
  are migrating data off some older disks\, onto new ones.  This extra act
 ivity is perceptible as sluggishness.  The migration is partly completed\
 , but will continue for some days.\nPlease use the /project filesystem as 
 your primary storage - this is the design and policy on all national syste
 ms.  /scratch is only ever intended for transient\, temporary files: if y
 ou can re-download or re-generate the file\, it is probably appropriate fo
 r /scratch.  You should not use /scratch as your normal or default storag
 e.  The current performance problem is at least partly due people attempt
 ing to defeat the 60-day /scratch expiration policy.\n\nhttps://status.all
 iancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1140
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1140
END:VEVENT
