BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Cedar] /nearline filesystem problem - Problème avec le système 
 de fichiers /nearline
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20250402T221300
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20250611T210900
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-1301@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:UNPLANNED
DESCRIPTION:Please note /nearline filesystem has been migrated to new stor
 age\, but backend tape storage was not changes. There are issues with dire
 ct access to files on the tape due to incorrect attribute on file metadata
 . If you need to access these files\, you need to restore them first.\nTo 
 see if a files in on disk or on tape\, use lfs hsm_state <filename> if the
  output contains "released"\, it means the file is on tape\, then use lfs 
 hsm_restore <filename> to restore it from tape to disk and then you can ha
 ve full access to the original content. These commands can be issued on ce
 dar login nodes and they are nonblocking. You can continue using "lfs hsm_
 state" to see if files are restored (no more "released" in the output).\nN
 ote : A restore may ake up to 4-5 hours before the file is actually restor
 ed depening on busy the backup system is.\nWe are still working on options
  to see if such issue can be fixed on the server end.\nTo prevent copying 
 zero size files without user attention\, we disabled /nearline access on G
 lobus cedar end point.\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?inci
 dent=1301
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1301
END:VEVENT
