BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Cedar] Planned Compute Outage on Cedar – April 29\, 2025
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20250429T070000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20250429T030000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-1313@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:As part of the preparations for bringing new equipment online\
 , a planned outage is scheduled for Tuesday\, April 29\, 2025\, from 7:00 
 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. (PDT) to support infrastructure work.\nDuring this windo
 w:\nCedar compute resources will be unavailable.\nJobs can still be submit
 ted\, but they will not run until after the outage is complete.\nOther Ced
 ar services (e.g.\, login nodes and storage) are currently expected to rem
 ain available.\nCedar cloud will remain operational.\nNo action is require
 d\, but please plan accordingly for job scheduling.\nWe recognize that thi
 s may cause disruption for those relying on Cedar\, but these modification
 s are necessary to support the installation of the new system\, Fir\, whic
 h will provide even greater capacity and capabilities.\n\nhttps://status.a
 lliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1313
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1313
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Béluga] 2025-04-30 - Planned partial outage - Arrêt partiel pla
 nifié
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20250430T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20250430T130000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-1310@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:Scheduled electrical maintenance will require us to shut down 
 the compute nodes from 12 PM (noon) on April 30 until 12 PM (noon) on May 
 1\, 2025 (EDT).\nBecause the compute nodes will be offline during this per
 iod\, jobs that would have finished after 12 PM (EDT) on April 30 will rem
 ain queued until the compute nodes are back online.\nThe storage will rema
 in accessible through Globus and the login nodes.\n======\nUne maintenance
  électrique planifiée nous oblige à éteindre les nœuds de calcul à p
 artir de 12 h (midi) le 30 avril\, jusqu’à 12 h (midi) le 1 mai 202
 5 (HAE).\nPuisque les nœuds de calcul seront hors ligne durant toute cett
 e période\, les tâches qui devaient se terminer après le 30 avril à 12
  h (HAE) resteront en file d’attente jusqu’au retour en service.\nLes 
 systèmes de stockage resteront accessibles via Globus et les nœuds de co
 nnexion.\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1310
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1310
