BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Fir] Outage
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260716T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260716T170000
DTSTAMP:20260723T200557Z
UID:drac-incident-1667@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:Hello\, The Fir cluster is currently undergoing unscheduled ma
 intenance to apply kernel security updates. This work requires rebooting c
 ompute nodes and cannot be deferred.\nWhat to expect:\n- Some running jobs
  may be killed as nodes are drained and rebooted.\n- New job submissions w
 ill queue normally and start once nodes return to service.\n- Login nodes 
 may be unavailable during the update window.\nWe expect all work to be com
 plete by 4:00 PM today (Pacific). If your job was interrupted\, please res
 ubmit once the cluster is back in production.\nWe apologize for the short 
 notice and the disruption. Security updates of this severity have to be ap
 plied promptly.\nWe will send a follow-up message once the cluster is full
 y back in service.\nThank you for your patience\, Fir Cluster Operations D
 igital Research Alliance of Canada\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_i
 ncident?incident=1667
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1667
END:VEVENT
